      "currency": "GBP",
      "description": "The only scientifically validated HRV app that works without an external sensor. Measure for one minute in the morning with your phone camera, a chest strap, an Oura ring or a Coros watch, and see how your body is responding to training and to everything else in your life.\n\nNEW: a complete redesign. Cleaner screens, faster to use, a new baseline page and everything available in English, Italian, Spanish, German, French, Portuguese and Japanese.\n\nHOW IT WORKS\n• Measure for one minute after waking up: phone camera, Bluetooth chest strap (we recommend a Polar H10). Oura or Coros night data can be used instead.\n• See your HRV and resting heart rate together with your normal range, so you know what is typical for you\n• Get daily advice to adapt your training, based on objective measures of your physiology\n• Tag sleep, motivation, soreness, stress, alcohol, travel, sickness, the menstrual cycle and more, to learn what affects you\n\nINSIGHTS\n• Baseline: your 7-day HRV and resting heart rate against your normal range, to spot meaningful changes\n• Long-term HRV trends\n• Correlations between your physiology and your tags\n• Training load: fitness, fatigue and how you respond to training\n• VO2max estimates for runners and cyclists, linking Strava or TrainingPeaks, lactate threshold estimation and training zones\n• Training polarization, weekly and monthly summaries\n\nOTHER FEATURES\n• PPG signal shown during camera measurements, to check signal quality\n• RR-intervals shown in real time when measuring with a chest strap\n• Heart rate, AVNN, SDNN, rMSSD, pNN50, LF and HF\n• RR-interval artifact correction\n• Population comparisons\n• Data export and integrations with Strava, TrainingPeaks, Oura, Coros, Apple Health and others\n\nPHONE COMPATIBILITY\nThe app checks right away whether your phone's camera is supported. Most iPhones work very well, but models with flash and camera very far apart (e.g. the iPhone 18 Pro) are not recommended. In these cases we recommend a Polar H10 chest strap, the most accurate sensor for HRV measurement.\n\nYOUR DATA\nAll data is processed in the app. An account with your email keeps your data backed up and lets you restore it if you change phone.\n\nMore on HRV and how to use the app: https://marcoaltini.substack.com\nPrivacy Policy and Terms: https://www.hrv4training.com/privacy--terms.html\nTerms of Use (EULA): https://www.apple.com/legal/internet-services/itunes/dev/stdeula/",
